{"name":"Holland Tile","hex":"#dd9789","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of linen cloth, originally from Holland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holland"},{"term":"tile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A regularly-shaped slab of clay or other material, affixed to cover or decorate a surface, as in a roof-tile, glazed tile, stove tile, carpet tile, etc.","A rectangular graphic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with tiles.","To arrange in a regular pattern, with adjoining edges (applied to tile-like objects, graphics, windows in a computer interface)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holland","blocks":[{"text":"Holland is a geographical region and former province on the western coast of the Netherlands. From the 10th to the 16th century, Holland proper was a unified political region within the Holy Roman Empire as a county ruled by the counts of Holland. By the 17th century, the province of Holland had risen to become a maritime and economic power, dominating the other provinces of the newly independent Dutch Republic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Holland_position.svg/330px-Holland_position.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holland","wikidata":"Q102911"},{"title":"Tile","blocks":[{"text":"Tiles are usually thin, square rectangular coverings manufactured from hard-wearing material such as ceramic, stone, metal, baked clay, or even glass. They are generally fixed in place in an array to cover roofs, floors, walls, edges, or other objects such as tabletops. Alternatively, tile can sometimes refer to similar units made from lightweight materials such as perlite, wood, and mineral wool, typically used for wall and ceiling applications. In another sense, a tile is a construction tile or similar object, such as rectangular counters used in playing games. The word is derived from the French word tuile, which is, in turn, from the Latin word tegula, meaning a roof tile composed of fired clay, otherwise known as nga."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg/330px-Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tile","wikidata":"Q468402"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Netherlands by population density by province (2006)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANetherlands_Density.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/1280px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of Holland (1682)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Provincie_No